        "text_1443359991": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "user-1f15d09fdf@example.invalid",
          "topPadding": "3",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-1f15d09fdf@example.invalid",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Wed Nov 27 2024 22:42:02 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h3><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-8em\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\">Building native bee houses to support local bee populations</span></span></span></h3>\n<p>From California to New Jersey, many teams across the U.S. are passionate about supporting Planet Bee Foundation, a nonprofit that is dedicated to creating a green-minded generation by teaching people about the importance of bees as a pathway to STEM, conservation and innovations in agriculture. Teams learn about the significance of native bees, how to identify local bee species and how to assemble native bee houses to help sustain local wildlife in their community.</p>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Nov 27 2024 23:05:34 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true",
          "cq:responsive": {
